==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˌpʊt ˈɒn/}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-to put on.ogg|a=UK}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|<,,put>}} {{tlb|en|transitive}}

# {{senseid|en|don}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[don]] (clothing, equipment{{,}} or the like).
#: {{ux|en|Why don't you '''put on''' your jacket. It's cold.}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Genesis|22|5|passage=And Iacob vowed a vow, ſaying, If God will be with me, and will keepe me in this way that I goe, and will giue me bꝛead to eate, and raiment to '''put on'''.}}
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To decorate or dress (something) onto another person or a surface.
#: {{ux|en|I '''put''' a coat '''on''' my daughter.}}
#: {{ux|en|I '''put''' tinsel '''on''' the Christmas tree.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|transitive}} To [[fool]], [[kid]], [[deceive]].
#: {{ux|en|You must be '''putting''' me '''on'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|She's '''putting on''' that she's sicker than she really is.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[assume]], [[adopt]] or [[affect]]; to behave in a particular way as a [[pretense]].
#: {{ux|en|Why are you '''putting''' that silly voice '''on'''?}}
#: {{ux|en|He's just '''putting on''' that limp -- his leg's actually fine.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[play]] (a [[recording]]).
#: {{ux|en|I'll '''put''' your favorite record '''on'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can you '''put on''' ''The Sound of Music''? I'd like to see it again.}}
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To play (a recording) on (a sound system).
#: {{ux|en|I'll '''put''' blues '''on''' the stereo.}}
#: {{ux|en|We usually '''put''' the Beatles '''on''' on my boombox.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To initiate [[cook]]ing or [[warm]]ing, especially on a [[stovetop]].
#: {{ux|en|I'll '''put on''' some coffee for everybody.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[perform]] for an audience.
#: {{ux|en|The actors '''put on''' a show last Saturday.}}
#: {{ux|en|The actors will '''put''' ''{{w|Macbeth}}'' '''on''' only one more time.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To organize a [[performance]] for an audience.
#: {{ux|en|The theatre company is  '''putting on''' ''Into the Woods'' this season.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]].
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To [[bet]] (money or other items) on (something).
#: {{ux|en|I '''put''' five pounds '''on''' that racehorse.}}
# {{lb|en|ditransitive}} To assign or apply (something) to a target.
#: {{ux|en|The gang boss '''put''' some goons '''on''' the other gang.}}
#: {{ux|en|The witch '''put''' a hex '''on''' me.}}
#: {{ux|en|This '''put'''s a completely different hue '''on''' the matter.}}
#: {{ux|en|Carl has been '''put on''' the [[front desk]] for tonight's shift.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To give (someone) a role in popular media.
#: {{ux|en|I hope they '''put''' me '''on''' TV.}}
#: {{ux|en|They '''put''' her '''on''' a billboard.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To set (movie, show, song, etc.) to play on a screen.
#: ''I '''put''' ''[[w:SpongeBob SquarePants|SpongeBob]]'' '''on''' when the kid gets fussy.''
# {{lb|en|transitive|dated}} To [[switch on]] (a device).
#* {{RQ:Bramah Eyes of Max Carrados|passage="Then the meter had been '''put on''' again?"}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[gain]] (weight).
#: {{ux|en|I '''put on''' at least five kilos over the holidays.}}
# {{&lit|en|put|on}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''put''' the pen '''on''' the table.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Put''' it '''on''' the list.}}
#: {{ux|en|The doctor '''put''' me '''on''' a diet.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete|intransitive}} To [[hurry up]]; to move [[swiftly]] forward.
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones
|passage=Sophia {{...}} saw several horses coming after on full speed. This greatly alarmed her fears, and she called to the guide to '''put on''' as fast as possible.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|literal—on a list}} {{l|en|put down}}; see also [[Thesaurus:enlist]]
* {{sense|don clothing}} {{l|en|beclothe}}; see also [[Thesaurus:clothe]]
